## 2. Task Model – Tables

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1: Navigate to Storage** | Robot moves to the storage location where the resource is located. | AND | storage | 1 | Only one robot can physically navigate to the storage. |
| **AT2: Request Resource** | Robot sends a message to the storage specifying the required resources. | AND | storage | 1 | The requesting robot must be the one that sends the request. |
| **AT3: Wait for Retrieval** | Robot waits until the requested resources are retrieved from storage. | AND | storage | 1 | The robot must idle until the storage confirms retrieval. |
| **AT4: Navigate to Delivery Location** | Robot moves to the specified delivery location. | AND | destination | 1 | One robot performs the transport to the destination. |
| **AT5: Deliver Resource** | Robot delivers the collected resources to the destination. | AND | destination | 1 | Final action of the delivery phase. |
| **AT6: Recharge at Station** | Robot goes to the recharging station to recharge its battery. | AND | recharge station | 1 | Only the robot with low battery can recharge. |
| **AT7: Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Robot assigns the remaining mission to another robot. | AND | base | 1 | The robot that detected low battery must hand over the remaining task. |
| **AT8: Return Resource to Checkpoint** | Robot returns the resource to a checkpoint during low battery in delivery. | AND | checkpoint | 1 | The robot must bring the resource to a safe location. |
| **AT9: Trigger Alert** | Robot triggers an alert and sends report to sector manager if it fails to return to checkpoint. | AND | sector manager | 1 | Only the robot that fails to return will trigger the alert. |

