## 4. Logical Relationships

| **Parent** | **Children** | **Relation** | **Runtime** | **Justification** |
|------------|--------------|--------------|-------------|-------------------|
| **G1** | G2, G9 | AND | `;` (sequential) | Both collection and delivery must be completed; the phases must occur one after the other. |
| **G2** | G3, G7 | AND | `FALLBACK(G3, G7)` | Normal collection proceeds via G3; if battery <10 % the robot switches to battery‑low handling G7. |
| **G3** | G4, G5, G6 | AND | `;` | Navigation → request → wait must happen in order. |
| **G4** | AT1 | AND | `-` | Single action performed by the robot. |
| **G5** | AT2 | AND | `-` | Single action performed by the robot. |
| **G6** | AT3 | AND | `-` | Single action performed by the robot. |
| **G7** | G8 | AND | `;` | Battery‑low handling requires recharging and assignment in sequence. |
| **G8** | AT6, AT7 | AND | `;` | Recharge first, then assign remaining mission. |
| **G9** | G10, G13 | AND | `FALLBACK(G10, G13)` | Normal delivery proceeds via G10; if battery <30 % the robot switches to battery‑low handling G13. |
| **G10** | G11, G12 | AND | `;` | Navigation → delivery must happen in order. |
| **G11** | AT4 | AND | `-` | Single action performed by the robot. |
| **G12** | AT5 | AND | `-` | Single action performed by the robot. |
| **G13** | G14, G15 | AND | `;` | Battery‑low handling requires return to checkpoint, assignment, and possibly alert. |
| **G14** | AT8, AT7 | AND | `;` | Return to checkpoint first, then assign remaining mission. |
| **G15** | AT9 | AND | `-` | Single action performed when return fails. |

